# 6529 Town settings. Copy this file to config.env (it is in .gitignore), fill in what you need, then: chmod 600 config.env
# daily.sh and capture.sh read config.env by themselves; lines starting with # are off.
# To run another script alone, load the settings first:  set -a; . ./config.env; set +a
# Every line must be empty, a # comment, or NAME=value. A value with & ; ( ) $ or spaces must stand in single
# quotes (a value in double quotes cannot hold $ ` or \). daily.sh and capture.sh stop on any other line and
# name it by its number, without showing it; the manual load above does show a broken line on your screen.

# --- Reading your validator -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The town reads the local page of YOUR OWN validator. The link to that page is an ADMIN link:
# never share it, never log it, never put it into a file that leaves your machine.
# The link must start with http://127.0.0.1: (if the validator runs on another machine, forward its local
# page to 127.0.0.1 on this one, for example with "ssh -L").
# Pick ONE of the three ways (the first that is set wins):
#TOWN_LINK='http://127.0.0.1:PORT/...'                  # the link itself (it changes when the validator restarts)
#TOWN_LINK_CMD="my-command-that-prints-the-link"        # any command that prints the link
# (other users of this machine can see that command while it runs, not what it prints: keep secrets out of it)
#VALIDATOR_BIN=validator                                # the validator program, asked with "open --print" (the default)

# --- Headless browser (reads the validator page, draws the link-preview picture) --------------------
CHROME_PATH=/path/to/chrome-or-chrome-headless-shell
#PUPPETEER_CORE=/path/to/node_modules/puppeteer-core    # only if "npm install" was not run in this folder
#NOBLE_BLAKE3=/path/to/node_modules/@noble/hashes/blake3.js

# --- Cloudflare Pages (optional: leave these off and daily.sh builds and checks the site but does not upload it) ---
#CF_PROJECT=my-town
#CF_TOKEN_FILE=/path/to/cloudflare-token.txt            # this file holds only the API token (permission "Cloudflare Pages: Edit")
#CF_ACCOUNT_FILE=/path/to/cloudflare-account.txt        # this file holds only your Cloudflare account ID (32 letters and digits)
# Keep both files outside this folder, readable only by you (chmod 600).

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Discord message when a run fails (once per day). The file holds: {"alertWebhook": "https://discord.com/api/webhooks/..."}
# Keep it outside this folder, readable only by you (chmod 600).
#TOWN_ALERT_WEBHOOK_FILE=/path/to/webhook.json
# The three posters on the main stage (the top of the public 6529.io ranking). The fetcher runs as user
# "nobody" in a systemd sandbox, so daily.sh must then run as root, and it needs a root-owned copy of
# stage_fetch.py outside your home folder and a folder that "nobody" may write.
# Leave both off and the town simply has no posters.
#TOWN_STAGE_DIR=/var/lib/mytown/stage
#TOWN_STAGE_FETCH=/opt/mytown/stage_fetch.py
# A history file for one extra cross-check in audit.py (one JSON object per line). Needed only when data/days-old-chain.json holds records.
#TOWN_NETWORK_HISTORY=/path/to/network-history.jsonl
# The bell (see "The bell (optional)" in README.md). With bell-public.json in this folder, daily.sh runs bell/bell-ring.py
# after each upload. This file holds only the ring key (the same text as the worker's RING_KEY secret, 32 to 256
# characters). Keep it outside this folder, readable only by you (chmod 600). Not set: the sender skips its run.
#TOWN_BELL_KEY_FILE=/path/to/bell-ring-key.txt
